    answer: 'Taraweeh is the extra night prayer of Ramadan, prayed after Isha, usually in congregation at the masjid. It is a strongly recommended sunnah, not an obligation. It is prayed two rak\'ahs at a time.\n\nHow many rak\'ahs: the schools and communities differ, and all of it is accepted.\n- Eight rak\'ahs plus witr (eleven in all): this follows A\'ishah\'s account that the Prophet ﷺ never prayed more than eleven rak\'ahs at night, in Ramadan or outside it (Sahih al-Bukhari 1147).\n- Twenty rak\'ahs plus witr: the view of the Hanafi, Shafi\'i and Hanbali schools, and what many masjids follow. Praying taraweeh together behind one reciter goes back to Umar, who gathered the people for it in Ramadan (Sahih al-Bukhari 2010).\n\nYou may pray it at home alone if you cannot reach the masjid. Praying longer with a calm, unhurried recitation matters more than the number.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1147, 2010.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-taraweeh]',
