    answer: 'The five daily prayers have 17 obligatory (fard) rak\'ahs: Fajr 2, Dhuhr 4, Asr 4, Maghrib 3, Isha 4. On Friday, Jumu\'ah (2 rak\'ahs with the khutbah) takes the place of Dhuhr. A traveller shortens the four-rak\'ah prayers to 2.\n\nAlongside them are the regular sunnah prayers (rawatib). The Prophet ﷺ promised a house in Paradise for twelve of them each day: four before Dhuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha and two before Fajr (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 415, sahih per Darussalam). The two before Fajr are the most emphasised. The schools differ on which are strongly emphasised and on extra ones (for example, four before Asr), so follow your school.\n\nWitr (odd rak\'ahs after Isha) is separate; see the Witr guide.\n\nSource: Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 415, sahih per Darussalam.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-nawafil]\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-witr]',
