    avoid: <String>[
      r'\b(?:quran|mushaf)\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Wudu is broken by what leaves the body and by loss of consciousness. All schools agree on these:\n- Urine, stool and wind (and the thin fluid called madhy). The Prophet ﷺ said the prayer of someone who has passed wind is not accepted until he makes wudu (Sahih al-Bukhari 135).\n- Deep sleep, fainting, madness or intoxication, anything that takes away your awareness. Safwan ibn Assal reported that on a journey the Prophet ﷺ told them to keep their socks on for three days, except for janabah, but not for urine, stool or sleep, meaning these need a fresh wudu (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 96, hasan per al-Albani).\n- Janabah (emission, intercourse) needs a full ghusl, not only wudu.\n\nLight dozing while sitting up, without losing awareness, does not break it. The Companions used to wait for the night prayer until they were nodding off, and then prayed without a new wudu (Sunan Abu Dawud 200, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nSleeping lying down or leaning breaks it. The schools differ on whether it also breaks when you sleep sitting firmly on the ground.\n\nThe schools differ on these:\n- Touching your private part with the hand: it breaks wudu in the Shafi\'i and Hanbali schools (and in the Maliki school if with desire); not in the Hanafi school.\n- Touching a woman\'s skin: it breaks wudu in the Shafi\'i school; in the Maliki and Hanbali schools only if with desire; not in the Hanafi school.\n- Flowing blood or a big vomit: it breaks wudu in the Hanafi school and, if a lot, in the Hanbali school; not in the Shafi\'i and Maliki schools.\n- Eating camel meat: it breaks wudu in the Hanbali school (Sahih Muslim 360).\n\nIf you doubt whether you broke it, leave the doubt: your wudu stays. The Prophet ﷺ said that a man who imagines he has broken wind in prayer should not leave unless he hears a sound or smells something (Sahih al-Bukhari 137).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 135, 137; Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 96, hasan per al-Albani; Sunan Abu Dawud 200, sahih per al-Albani; Sahih Muslim 360.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-wudu]',
    topic: 'wudu',
    beforeGate: true,
    why: 'These are the things that make a person need a fresh wudu, because they are a state of impurity from the body.',
